  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When searching for a variable to add, it is called a float. But in the case of an array, it is called a single[]. However once adding a single[], it will appear in the inspector as a float[]. Similar problems exist with int16 vs short and int64 vs long. This inconsistency makes them difficult to search for if you don't know the correct name. It may even lead you to believe that the type of variable you're looking for doesn't exist.",
